# PROJECT: MODERN DEVELOPER PORTFOLIO WEBSITE

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, frontend architect, and web performance specialist.

Your mission is to design and build a complete, modern, professional, responsive, and production-ready personal portfolio website for a fictional computer science student interested in software development, web technologies, computer networks, and cybersecurity.

The website must have a premium visual identity, smooth animations, excellent usability, clean code, and a fully responsive layout.

The entire project must be compatible with deployment on Vercel.

Use the following technologies when appropriate:

* Next.js with the App Router.
* React.
* TypeScript.
* Tailwind CSS.
* Lucide React for icons.
* Framer Motion or Motion for animations, provided the chosen version is compatible with the project dependencies.

Use Google AI Studio to generate the project files and implementation.

IMPORTANT: Do not create a simple mockup or a static landing page. Build a complete, coherent website with reusable components, functional navigation, accessible interactions, and a clear project structure.

Do not stop after generating a homepage preview. Implement the complete website and all required files.

If a technical decision is necessary, choose the most reliable, maintainable, and Vercel-compatible solution.

